A||||8||Tom88gt||power antenna install?||||5||
Z||000000||Tom88gt||06-09-2001||11:07 AM||||I want to install a power antenna in the factory location.  Has anyone done this and how was the clearance under the fender?  The diagram in the Haynes manual looks like the inner fender (steel frame) is directly below the hole, thus preventing the antenna and power unit from mounting directly under the hole.<P>I did an archive search and didn't come up with anything other than a 300ZX type install???||||reg||5
Z||000001||cadaver||06-09-2001||01:33 PM||||Yes the steel is directly onder the fender. The factory antenna has a flat pad with two bolt that mount to that steel frame. You could drill a hole through it but I dont know how much room there is under it. Just pull the fender. They come off easy.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Uaana||06-09-2001||02:25 PM||||I'm in the middle of reassembling my SE and Just put the fenders back on. It doesn't look like there would be an easy way to mount a motor in the area under the stock location. If you are looking for cleaner lines you might want to look into installing a tape antenne on the windshield and just covering the stock hole. <BR>Just a thought.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||06-09-2001||03:43 PM||||Anyone have a link to the thread discussing the installation of a power antenna in the rear deck area??<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tom88gt||06-10-2001||11:32 AM||||There is a teal green coupe down in the Gulfport area that has a power antenna install in the rear pillar.  Very nice job.  I don't know the owner but he belongs to Gold Coast Fiero.  If you can track him down he can probably help you out.||||reg||4
Z||000005||mbramble||06-10-2001||12:07 PM||||I have installed one about 2" back from the stock location.  With the unit I bought, putting it in the stock location would have required cutting a clearance hole in the inner wheel well liner.  Moving it back took care of that.  I have yet to fill in the original hole in the fender and drill a new one as the car has a lot more to be done before it gets to that point in re-assembly.  The only real problem I have is that the antenna, when fully retracted, is below the fender.  I have found a piece to put on top of the antenna to bring it up to the level of the fender so there isn't just an empty hole there when the antenna is down.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Tom88gt||06-11-2001||09:40 AM||||Why not just cut the clearance hole in the inner fender liner?  Or would this have caused other problems?||||reg||5
Z||000007||mbramble||06-11-2001||02:43 PM||||I did not want to see the power antenna motor unit prodruding into the wheel well...||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||06-11-2001||07:38 PM||||Asside from looking like hell....<P>Main Problem... the antena probably would not last long exposed to the wheel well. They are sealed but not so well they'd take that for long. It's going to have all kinds of dirt and water on it there...||||reg||1
